# Requirements Engineering

Own requirement quality only. Keep each statement precise, measurable,
traceable, allocated, and verification-ready. Do not persist SDoc. Do not
choose models or lineups. Remain workflow-neutral.

## Match

Match: author or check a requirement, apply the NASA-adapted checklist, or
record a quality-gate result.

Non-match: SDoc or SysON persistence or publication; model or lineup choice;
SysML modeling; product tests; skill authoring.

## Inputs and preconditions

Candidate statement, parent IDs, allocation target, and intended verification
method. Require
[standards receipts](../engineering-methods/references/standards-receipts.md). Cite those
rows. Invent no ISO 29148 clauses.

## Procedure

1. On persistence, lineup, test-code, or skill-authoring requests, return
   `TYPED_GAP_RS_PERSISTENCE`, `TYPED_GAP_LINEUP`, `TYPED_GAP_TEST_CODE`, or
   `TYPED_GAP_SKILL_AUTHORING`. Write nothing.
2. Author with [requirements-authoring](references/requirements-authoring.md). Do not run the
   checklist in this step.
3. Check with [nasa-requirement-checklist](references/nasa-requirement-checklist.md). Map every concern
   to an AlphaZede rule, check type, typed failure, and evidence.
4. Gate with [quality-gate](references/quality-gate.md). Record pass or typed failures.
5. For an interface obligation, fill
   [interface-completeness-profile](references/interface-completeness-profile.md)
   (IFACE-PROFILE-EMV-001): one disposition per field; blank `APPLICABLE` and
   rationale-free `NOT_APPLICABLE` fail; unknowns stay visible `GAP`. Define
   obligations only; do not represent, test, or assemble.
6. Return the statement, checklist results, and gate record. Hand persistence
   to Requirements System.

## Bounds

Three correction rounds. Stop on typed gap, missing S8 receipt, or exhausted
rounds.

## Outcomes

`PASS`, `FAIL` with typed failures, `TYPED_GAP`, `BLOCKED`.
