# Requirements authoring

Write the statement. Do not apply the NASA-adapted checklist here. Do not
record a quality-gate verdict here. Do not persist SDoc, SysON, or any
register. Do not choose models or lineups.

Authority: CONTRACT-EMV-004 and DEC-EMV-007. This method owns quality of the
statement. Requirements System owns stored content, relationships, revision,
validation, review, and publication. Bearing Lite owns execution planning and
lineup. Test Engineering owns V&V method selection for the realized system.
Cite S8 `SRC-EMV-COE`. Do not invent ISO 29148 clauses (`SRC-EMV-29148`
metadata-only).

## Inputs

- Candidate need in the requester's words
- Parent or scope IDs when they exist
- Allocation target (element, procedure, or layer)
- Intended verification method from analysis, inspection, demonstration,
  test, or evaluation (COE-ELSD-064)
- S8 file [standards-receipts.md](../../engineering-methods/references/standards-receipts.md)

Stop with `BLOCKED` if S8 is missing. Stop with `TYPED_GAP_RS_PERSISTENCE` or
`TYPED_GAP_LINEUP` if the request is persistence or lineup choice.

## Write the five attributes

Produce one statement that is all five at once.

**Precise.** Name the subject that must act. Use one binding obligation. Say
the need, not the design, not the operator procedure, not a work assignment.
Keep one thought: one subject, one action, one object. Prefer an affirmative
duty. Define every technical term or point to a glossary. Do not hedge.

**Measurable.** State a quantity, bound, identity, or other observable that a
later check can read without invention. If a value is still open, record the
placeholder with owner, close-by date, and what evidence will close it. Do
not ship an unbounded quality adjective as if it were a measure.

**Traceable.** Assign a unique ID. Name parent or scope IDs so the statement
resolves both up and down (COE-ELSD-062, AC-EMV-009). Record a short
rationale and any assumption. A statement with no parent and no scope ID is
not yet a requirement.

**Allocated.** Name the element, procedure, or layer that must satisfy it.
Keep the allocation at the correct level. Do not park a product duty on a
person, a plan, or the Requirements System unless that is the actual subject.
This skill's output is a candidate statement, not the register.

**Verification-ready.** Name one method from analysis, inspection,
demonstration, test, or evaluation, and the verification-case identity, before
implementation of that requirement (COE-ELSD-014, COE-ELSD-064). The case
carries a positive case, a negative case, and a named executable check.
Pass/fail must be stateable from the statement plus that case. This method
does not write product tests.

## Required fields

Emit these fields with the statement:

| field | rule |
| --- | --- |
| `id` | Unique, stable, citable |
| `statement` | Binding sentence meeting the five attributes |
| `parent_ids` | Parent or scope identities; empty only with a recorded gap |
| `allocation` | Named satisfying element, procedure, or layer |
| `verification_method` | One of the five COE-ELSD-064 methods |
| `verification_case_id` | Identity of the prospective case |
| `positive_case` | Observable success |
| `negative_case` | Observable failure the check can detect |
| `named_check` | Repeatable inspection, analysis, or other named check |
| `rationale` | Why the need exists |
| `assumptions` | Explicit; unconfirmed assumptions stay open |

Do not store these fields in SDoc from this skill. Hand the candidate to
Requirements System when persistence is requested.

## S8 citations

| row_id | fields used here |
| --- | --- |
| SRC-EMV-COE | source AlphaZede COE; tailored; precedence 2; retrieval_date 2026-09-09; full-text; cite UIDs COE-ELSD-014, COE-ELSD-016, COE-ELSD-062, COE-ELSD-064; do not copy COE body |
| SRC-EMV-29148 | RE process and information-item family; 2018 Edition 2; metadata-only; no clause inventory |
| SRC-EMV-NASA-SEH | named Appendix C exists; authoring stays separate from that checklist (DEC-EMV-004) |

ISO/IEC/IEEE DIS 29148 (`SRC-EMV-29148-DIS`) is watch-only. INCOSE SEH v5
(`SRC-EMV-INCOSE-SEH-V5`) is metadata-only practitioner guidance and is not
this authoring method.
