# Requirement quality gate

Run this file after authoring and after the NASA-adapted checklist. Do not
author here. Do not merge checklist concerns into the authoring method. Do
not persist SDoc or SysON. Do not choose models or lineups. Do not write
product tests.

Cite S8 rows `SRC-EMV-NASA-SEH`, `SRC-EMV-COE`, and `SRC-EMV-29148`
(metadata-only, no clauses). This gate is a procedure, not a register
(DES-EMV-022, AC-EMV-008).

## Preconditions

- Candidate statement plus the authoring fields from
  [requirements-authoring.md](requirements-authoring.md)
- Checklist file [nasa-requirement-checklist.md](nasa-requirement-checklist.md)
- S8 receipts present
- Request is not persistence, lineup choice, or product-test authoring

If the request is persistence, return `TYPED_GAP_RS_PERSISTENCE` and write
nothing. If it is lineup choice, return `TYPED_GAP_LINEUP`. If it is product
tests, return `TYPED_GAP_TEST_CODE`.

## Procedure

1. Load every `CHK-RE-*` row. Skipping a row is `FAIL` unless the record
   marks `N/A` with a scope reason.
2. For each row, apply the named check type to the candidate and record
   `PASS`, `FAIL`, or `N/A`.
3. On `FAIL`, record the row's typed failure and the evidence string. Do not
   invent a new failure code.
4. On `N/A`, record the reason. A blank reason becomes `FAIL`.
5. Aggregate:
   - `PASS` if every row is `PASS` or justified `N/A`
   - `FAIL` if any row is `FAIL`
6. Return the record below. Hand persistence to Requirements System. Do not
   treat this record as SDoc, review, or publication.

Three correction rounds may re-author and re-check. Stop when the gate
passes, a typed gap applies, S8 is missing, or rounds are exhausted.

## Record

```text
gate: requirements-engineering/quality-gate
candidate_id: <id>
authoring_file: references/requirements-authoring.md
checklist_file: references/nasa-requirement-checklist.md
s8_rows: SRC-EMV-NASA-SEH, SRC-EMV-COE, SRC-EMV-29148
verdict: PASS | FAIL | TYPED_GAP | BLOCKED
typed_failures: <codes or none>
typed_gap: <code or none>
rows:
  - id: CHK-RE-NN
    result: PASS | FAIL | N/A
    typed_failure: <code or none>
    evidence: <observable>
    na_reason: <reason or none>
```

## Typed gaps (not gate failures)

| code | request | owner |
| --- | --- | --- |
| TYPED_GAP_RS_PERSISTENCE | write, revise, validate, review, or publish SDoc/SysON | `use-requirements-system` |
| TYPED_GAP_LINEUP | choose harness, model, or lineup | Bearing Lite |
| TYPED_GAP_TEST_CODE | write product tests | Test Engineering / `write-tests` |
| TYPED_GAP_SKILL_AUTHORING | create or revise a skill | `create-lean-skill` |
