# Interface completeness profile — IFACE-PROFILE-EMV-001

One shared profile for interface completeness, used by Requirements
Engineering, SysML Modeling, Test Engineering, and Integration Engineering.
It is a reference inside the existing methods (DES-EMV-037). It is **not** a
tool, not a normative store, not a second requirements register, and not a
mandatory sixth planning artifact. Requirement identity and change authority
stay in the current authority of record.

This profile paraphrases the public NASA SEH Appendix L interface-requirements
outline concern set (`SRC-EMV-NASA-APPENDIX-L`, DEC-EMV-048). It is not that
appendix, does not reproduce its body, and claims no NASA conformance. It also
claims no ISO clause coverage (`SRC-EMV-29148`, `SRC-EMV-24748-6` are
metadata-only).

## S8 citations (DEC-EMV-003 fields relied on)

| row_id | source | issuer | edition / page identity | URL | retrieval_date | status | precedence | mismatch | derived rule | evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| SRC-EMV-NASA-APPENDIX-L | NASA SEH Appendix L, Interface Requirements Document outline | NASA, Office of the Chief Engineer | nasa.gov reference page, WP reference id 262967; published 2019-10-17; page last updated 2023-07-26 | https://www.nasa.gov/reference/appendix-l-interface-requirements-document-outline/ | 2026-09-09 | informative | 8 | Page prints no SP number or revision letter; alignment with `SRC-EMV-NASA-SEH` (SP-2016-6105 Rev2) is unverified | Paraphrase the outline's concern set into AlphaZede fields, dispositions, and typed failures; do not copy body; claim no NASA conformance | S8-format retrieval receipt in this file |
| SRC-EMV-NASA-SEH | NASA Systems Engineering Handbook | NASA, Office of the Chief Engineer | NASA/SP-2016-6105 Rev2 | https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/nasa_systems_engineering_handbook_0.pdf | 2026-09-09 | informative | 8 | See `SRC-EMV-NASA-APPENDIX-L` alignment mismatch | Name appendices; do not copy them | S8 full-text PDF receipt; access_class full-text |
| SRC-EMV-COE | AlphaZede COE libraries | AlphaZede | `docs/coe/index.md` plus ELSD/ASA `.sdoc` as in S8 | repository://Alphazedehq/docs/coe/index.md | 2026-09-09 | tailored | 2 | S8 records index-pin vs worktree ELSD digest mismatch | Cite COE UIDs; owner decisions outrank COE | S8 full-text UID grep |
| SRC-EMV-24748-6 | ISO/IEC/IEEE 24748-6:2023 integration guidance | ISO, IEC, IEEE | 2023 Edition 1 | https://www.iso.org/standard/81563.html | 2026-09-09 | informative | 6 | none versus DEC-EMV-002 | Process-family citation only; invent no clauses | S8 access_class metadata-only |

## Dispositions

Every required field carries **exactly one** disposition.

| disposition | required content | typed failure when missing |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `APPLICABLE` | nonblank value **and** evidence pointer | `BLANK_APPLICABLE_VALUE` |
| `NOT_APPLICABLE` | scope rationale **and** evidence pointer | `UNJUSTIFIED_NOT_APPLICABLE` |
| `GAP` | missing information, owner, affected claim, closure condition | `INCOMPLETE_GAP_RECORD` |

Rules:

1. Blank `APPLICABLE` values fail. Whitespace, `TBD`, and `-` are blank.
2. A rationale-free or evidence-free `NOT_APPLICABLE` fails.
3. An unknown required value stays a visible `GAP`. It is never silently
   dropped, downgraded to `NOT_APPLICABLE`, or absorbed into prose.
4. A `GAP` blocks **only** the compatibility or execution claim it affects.
   Unaffected claims stay evaluable.
5. Zero or two dispositions on one field fail (`MULTIPLE_DISPOSITIONS`).
6. A composite field covers several topics. Record one disposition per covered
   topic, then one roll-up disposition for the field: `GAP` when any covered
   topic holds an open `GAP`; `APPLICABLE` when every covered topic is
   `APPLICABLE` or justified `NOT_APPLICABLE` and at least one is `APPLICABLE`;
   `NOT_APPLICABLE` when every covered topic is justified `NOT_APPLICABLE`. The
   topic dispositions stay visible. A roll-up that hides one is `HIDDEN_UNKNOWN`.
   Rule 4 still bounds what the gap blocks.

## Required fields

| field | topics it must cover | notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `purpose_and_scope` | why the interface exists and what it bounds | |
| `precedence` | which document controls on conflict | |
| `applicable_and_reference_sources` | binding sources versus referenced sources | |
| `endpoint_identities_and_responsibilities` | endpoint identity; responsibilities and ownership per side | |
| `exchanged_data_signals_or_quantities` | exchanges and direction per item | |
| `types_shapes_units_limits_timing_and_protocol` | data types and structure; units and conventions; limits and tolerances; timing and performance; protocol and transport | composite; rule 6 roll-up |
| `initialization_states_errors_and_recovery` | initialization and shutdown; states and modes; errors and fault containment; recovery and resynchronization | composite; rule 6 roll-up |
| `authoritative_requirement_ids` | requirement links into the authority of record | unresolved link → `UNRESOLVED_LINK` |
| `model_relationships_or_selected_mode_disposition` | model links, or the selected modeling mode and why no link exists | unresolved link → `UNRESOLVED_LINK` |
| `positive_and_negative_verification_cases` | verification links; both expectations per applicable obligation | one-sided case → `CASE_WITHOUT_NEGATIVE` |
| `gaps` | the open `GAP` records and what each blocks | |

## Three separate verdicts

Never merge these. Each cites evidence of its own class (RISK-EMV-016).

| verdict | question | admissible evidence | inadmissible |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| structural completeness | does every required field carry a valid disposition? | this profile's field-by-field check record | runtime logs |
| semantic compatibility | do both endpoints' obligations agree in meaning? | both sides' obligations compared field by field | a filled profile, a JSON Schema pass, or a diagram |
| connected runtime evidence | does the assembled interface behave as required? | positive and negative cases run on the exact candidate | a mock, a stub, or a schema pass |

A profile pass is structural completeness only. It is not compatibility and not
runtime proof.

## Responsibility allocation

One bounded input, output, and prohibition per role (DES-EMV-038,
AC-EMV-032). No role holds another's authority.

| role | owns | prohibition |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Requirements Engineering | defines interface obligations and applicability; fills field dispositions | does not represent, persist, test, or assemble |
| SysML Modeling | represents obligations and traces model elements to authoritative requirement IDs in the selected mode | does not change the Journey's `diagram-assisted` mode or `sysml_claim` false; does not become a register |
| Requirements System / SysON | governs authoritative persistence, query behavior, relationships, revisions, review, and publication boundaries | not superseded by this profile |
| Test Engineering | defines positive and negative cases for every `APPLICABLE` obligation | does not design the obligation or accept a mock as the acceptance article |
| Integration Engineering | checks compatibility against both endpoints and exercises the connected interface | does not self-certify or treat a profile pass as runtime proof |
| Plan Integrator | consumes resulting evidence into the existing five planning artifacts | not an entry point for filling this profile |

## Profile check — PROC-INTERFACE-PROFILE-CHECK

Inspect the record field by field and return structural completeness only.

Typed failures: `BLANK_APPLICABLE_VALUE`, `UNJUSTIFIED_NOT_APPLICABLE`,
`INCOMPLETE_GAP_RECORD`, `MULTIPLE_DISPOSITIONS`, `HIDDEN_UNKNOWN`,
`UNRESOLVED_LINK`, `CASE_WITHOUT_NEGATIVE`.

Outcomes: exactly one of `PROFILE_COMPLETE`,
`PROFILE_COMPLETE_WITH_GAPS`, or `PROFILE_INCOMPLETE` with typed failures.

## Fixtures

`FIX-IFACE-01` is the representative application. `FIX-IFACE-02` through
`FIX-IFACE-04` are deliberate check fixtures for the procedure. They are not
interface claims and carry no requirement values of their own.

### FIX-IFACE-01 — representative application (expected `PROFILE_COMPLETE_WITH_GAPS`)

Existing Requirements System Local stdio interface. Values are those recorded
in `seit.json` `interface_completeness_profile.representative_application`;
execution rebinds the then-current source, package, managed-specification
revision, and digest before evidence collection.

| field | disposition | value / rationale | evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `purpose_and_scope` | `APPLICABLE` | Read-only identity query from a Local MCP client process to the packaged `alphazede-requirements-system` host process | AC-EMV-033 |
| `precedence` | `APPLICABLE` | Owner decisions, then COE, then external standards; DEC-EMV-048 controls this application | technical-plan Authority and precedence list |
| `applicable_and_reference_sources` | `APPLICABLE` | Binding: DEC-EMV-048, AUTH-EMV-INTERFACE-001. Reference: `SRC-EMV-NASA-APPENDIX-L`, `SRC-EMV-24748-6` | S8 receipts |
| `endpoint_identities_and_responsibilities` | `APPLICABLE` | Local MCP client process issues requests; packaged host process answers within register `alphazede.requirements-system.azedge` | `seit.json` representative_application |
| `exchanged_data_signals_or_quantities` | `APPLICABLE` | Request in: exactly one `scope` string matching the configured managed specification. Response out: register, source MID/revision/digest, requirement MID/UID pairs only | `seit.json` representative_application |
| `types_shapes_units_limits_timing_and_protocol` | `GAP` | Rule 6 roll-up. Topics — data types and structure `APPLICABLE`: JSON-RPC, one message per line, `requirements.query.v1`. Units and conventions `APPLICABLE`: byte counts and MID/UID identifiers; no physical units. Limits and tolerances `APPLICABLE`: `scope` max 128 bytes, request max 8192 bytes. Protocol and transport `APPLICABLE`: MCP protocol 2026-07-28 over Local stdio. Timing and performance `GAP`: see `GAP-IFACE-01` | `seit.json` representative_application; `GAP-IFACE-01` |
| `initialization_states_errors_and_recovery` | `APPLICABLE` | Rule 6 roll-up; all four topics `APPLICABLE`. Initialization and shutdown, states and modes: initialize, discover, list, call, EOF shutdown. Errors and fault containment: wrong register/scope/name/arguments, duplicate member, malformed or oversized frame, cancellation, service unavailability, and invalid receipt all fail closed with no mutation, fallback, or extra disclosure. Recovery and resynchronization: restart the Local process after a terminal input rejection | `seit.json` representative_application; SEIT-EMV-048 |
| `authoritative_requirement_ids` | `APPLICABLE` | AC-EMV-031, AC-EMV-032, AC-EMV-033; RISK-EMV-016, RISK-EMV-017 | technical plan; `design.md` traceability |
| `model_relationships_or_selected_mode_disposition` | `APPLICABLE` | Selected mode `diagram-assisted`, `sysml_claim` false. Diagrams are explanatory; no native SysML or SysON relation instance is claimed | DES-EMV-041 |
| `positive_and_negative_verification_cases` | `APPLICABLE` | Positive: valid discovery/list/call/EOF flow returns identity-only output. Negative: wrong scope and unknown tool refuse without mutation, fallback, or extra disclosure; duplicate, malformed, oversize, and cancellation coverage retained | SEIT-EMV-048 (cases defined; results not yet claimed) |
| `hardware interface planes` (topic under `types_…`) | `NOT_APPLICABLE` | No mechanical, fluid, power, coordinate, environmental, or physical human-operability plane exists at this process-only software/data boundary | `seit.json` representative_application `hardware_categories` |
| `gaps` | `APPLICABLE` | `GAP-IFACE-01` below | this file |

Open gap:

| gap | missing information | owner | affected claim | closure condition |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `GAP-IFACE-01` | No latency or throughput obligation is stated for the Local stdio call | Requirements Engineering | semantic compatibility and connected runtime evidence **for timing only** | RE states a timing obligation or records a justified `NOT_APPLICABLE`, then TE adds cases |

Verdicts for this fixture:

- structural completeness: `PROFILE_COMPLETE_WITH_GAPS`. Every required field
  carries exactly one disposition, including the rule 6 roll-up.
- semantic compatibility: **not claimed**; `GAP-IFACE-01` blocks the timing
  portion only. Identity, limits, protocol, and error behaviour stay evaluable.
- connected runtime evidence: **not claimed**; pending the SEIT-EMV-048
  exercise on the exact candidate.

### FIX-IFACE-02 — blank `APPLICABLE` (expected `PROFILE_INCOMPLETE`)

Same interface, with `exchanged_data_signals_or_quantities` marked
`APPLICABLE` and its value left as `TBD`.

Result: `PROFILE_INCOMPLETE`, typed failure `BLANK_APPLICABLE_VALUE` on
`exchanged_data_signals_or_quantities`. Rule 1. A blank value is not a
`GAP`; relabelling it `GAP` without owner, affected claim, and closure
condition yields `INCOMPLETE_GAP_RECORD`.

### FIX-IFACE-03 — unexplained `NOT_APPLICABLE` (expected `PROFILE_INCOMPLETE`)

Same interface, with `initialization_states_errors_and_recovery` marked
`NOT_APPLICABLE` and no rationale or evidence.

Result: `PROFILE_INCOMPLETE`, typed failure `UNJUSTIFIED_NOT_APPLICABLE`.
Rule 2. The disposition is admissible only with a scope rationale of the form
used for the hardware planes in `FIX-IFACE-01`.

### FIX-IFACE-04 — required unknown held as `GAP` (expected `PROFILE_COMPLETE_WITH_GAPS`)

Same interface, with the maximum request size unknown:
`types_shapes_units_limits_timing_and_protocol` rule 6 roll-up `GAP` — its
limits-and-tolerances topic is `GAP` while its other topics stay `APPLICABLE`.
Missing information "oversize frame threshold", owner Requirements Engineering,
affected claim "oversize-frame compatibility and its negative execution case",
closure condition "RE states the threshold; TE adds the oversize negative case".

Result: `PROFILE_COMPLETE_WITH_GAPS`. Structural completeness passes because
the `GAP` record is complete and visible. The gap blocks only the oversize
compatibility claim and its execution case. Identity, protocol, states, error
containment, and their cases stay evaluable. Erasing this gap, or reporting the
interface as compatible while it is open, is `HIDDEN_UNKNOWN`.

## Excluded follow-on

`alphazede/requirements-system#72` live SysML/SysON storage and enforcement and
`alphazede/bearing-dev#186` SEMP coordination remain outside this profile
(DES-EMV-041, CONTRACT-EMV-028). Neither is acceptance evidence here.
