#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Mechanical lint for COE StrictDoc requirement libraries.

Checks each `[REQUIREMENT]` node of every named `.sdoc` file against the
mechanical rules of CONTRACT-ELSD-001 and DEC-ELSD-022:

  UID_PATTERN        UID matches ^COE-[A-Z]{2,4}-\\d{3}$
  FIELD_MISSING      all 22 core fields (REQ-CORE-REQUIRED) are present
  TITLE_LENGTH       TITLE is at most 8 words
  EARS_ONE_SENTENCE  STATEMENT is exactly one sentence ending in a period
  EARS_PATTERN       STATEMENT opens with an EARS pattern keyword
  EARS_MODAL         STATEMENT carries a shall / should / may modal
  VERIFICATION_METHOD  every listed method is a recognized method
  BANNED_TERM        no NASA Appendix C unmeasured term in STATEMENT
  AGNOSTIC_TERM      no tool, role, or system name in STATEMENT
  GLOSSARY_REF       every glossary term used in STATEMENT is referenced by
                     its GLOSS-* identifier in CONSTRAINTS
  NODE_SEPARATOR     exactly one empty line required between nodes
  REQUIREMENT_CLASS  a present class label is product or process (azedge#126);
                     the five validation+class fields are required only when
                     the document declares the extension in METADATA

The noun-phrase half of the DEC-ELSD-022 title rule is not checked here: no
mechanical rule for it was found that does not misfire, so titles are held to
the word limit mechanically and to the noun-phrase form by review.

A document-level pass (DES-ASA-003) runs first, over the `[DOCUMENT]` node:

  DOC_TYPE_UNKNOWN     the declared governed type has no structural floor to
                       read, so the document cannot be checked and is failed
                       closed rather than passed silently
  DOC_ELEMENT_MISSING  a required structural floor element has no heading
  DOC_ELEMENT_EMPTY    a required element's heading carries no body

The floor itself is never listed here. It is declared in the CoE library and
read from it at runtime (DES-ASA-002), so changing an element is an edit to the
standard rather than to this tool. If the `[DOCUMENT]` METADATA `type` is not a
governed type the pass is a no-op and behaviour is exactly the requirement-level
behaviour above.

Every violation is reported as `<file>:<UID>: <rule>: <detail>`, and every
document-level violation as `<file>: <rule>: <detail>` — the same shape at
document scope.

For a governed document the lint prints exactly one conformance state
(DES-ASA-004): `FLOOR_INCOMPLETE` when floor elements are absent or empty or no
floor can be read at all, `CHECKS_FAILING` when the floor is satisfied but a
mechanical check fails, and `REVIEW_READY` when the file is mechanically clean.
The last two carry their own not-reviewed disclaimer. The mapping is total: a
governed document falls in exactly one of those three cases. The fourth
conformance state of the standard is an owner act, recorded outside this lint,
and is emitted by no code path here. An ungoverned document gets no state line,
exactly as before this pass existed.

A document may declare `lint_profile: project-specification` in its
`[DOCUMENT]` METADATA. That profile is for a project's own specification, whose
requirement statements are owner-approved text rather than CoE library
authoring: it keeps the document-level pass and the FIELD_MISSING,
TITLE_LENGTH and VERIFICATION_METHOD checks, and skips the library-authoring
rules (UID_PATTERN, the three EARS rules, BANNED_TERM, AGNOSTIC_TERM and
GLOSSARY_REF). Any other value, or no declaration, is the library profile and
behaves exactly as above.

A governed document may also declare `section_layout: COE-ASA-043` in its
`[DOCUMENT]` METADATA (Alphazedehq#219). It then adopts the section layout of
COE-ASA-043 through COE-ASA-046, and the mechanical parts are checked here. A
section runs from its floor heading to the next floor heading or the first
glossary entry:

  LAYOUT_UNKNOWN     section_layout names a layout this lint does not know
  SECTION_ORDER      a requirement follows the section's explanation, or the
                     figure is not in the section's last node
  FIGURE_COUNT       a section carries other than exactly one figure caption
  FIGURE_CLASS       a figure caption names a kind outside the figure classes
  TONE_SHALL         "shall" appears outside a requirement statement
  OPEN_PARAMETER     an open parameter lacks an owner, a close-by date or its
                     closure evidence
  SILENT_GAP         TBD, TBC, TODO, FIXME or "to be determined" appears
                     anywhere, including inside an open parameter; state the
                     value or its open parameter without the placeholder

A document without the declaration is checked exactly as before.

Exit 0 when clean, 1 on any violation, 2 when an input cannot be read.

This lint is deliberately stdlib-only and never mutates the tree.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import datetime
import os
