fail('AC-AFC-FEED-01','wording; traceability','CHK-RE-17 INCOMPLETE; CHK-RE-24 CONTRADICTION; CHK-RE-39 INTERFACE_INCONSISTENT','“normalize each ESPN play” into the six listed event types has no disposition for an ordinary non-triggering play and excludes the correction type required by FEED-02 and CONTRACT-AFC-EVENT.','The backend shall emit GameEvents for ESPN plays and game-state changes that meet the event definitions in DES-AFC-FEED, and for corrections required by AC-AFC-FEED-02, using CONTRACT-AFC-EVENT with source game id, source play id, event type, involved ESPN athlete ids, possession team, field position, period, game clock, source timestamp and ingest timestamp; it shall emit no GameEvent for a play that meets none of those definitions and shall reject a schema-invalid response without changing stored GameEvents.')
fail('AC-AFC-FEED-02','wording; measurability','CHK-RE-24 CONTRADICTION; CHK-RE-48 NO_PASS_FAIL','“at most one GameEvent per source game id and source play id” forbids the additional correction GameEvent required by the same sentence; “exactly one correction” does not distinguish repeated retrieval from successive corrections.','The backend shall emit at most one original GameEvent per source game id and source play id; when the recorded scoring content for that play changes, it shall emit one correction GameEvent for that change referencing the original event, and repeated retrieval of unchanged scoring content shall emit no additional event.')
fail('AC-AFC-ALERT-04','traceability; measurability','CHK-RE-24 CONTRADICTION; CHK-RE-30 INCORRECT; CHK-RE-35 UNREALISTIC_PERFORMANCE','“show each released alert as a heads-up notification” ignores CTRL-01’s panel-only setting; “within one alert_poll_wait” reuses a server request-wait bound as a physical-device latency guarantee despite #1’s explicit exclusion of hardware performance verification.','While a provider app plays video in the foreground and the customer is in an enabled viewing period with heads-up presentation selected, the TV app shall present each received released alert as a heads-up notification with Watch and Dismiss actions without bringing the companion app to the foreground; while panel-only presentation is selected, it shall suppress heads-up notifications.')
fail('AC-AFC-ALERT-05','undefined term; measurability','CHK-RE-25 GLOSSARY_MISMATCH; CHK-RE-49 VAGUE_TERM','“wording intensity follows the customer’s excitement level” supplies no observable mapping; DES-AFC-POLICY says three levels but does not define their template mapping.','The backend shall select alert text through a documented mapping from each customer-selectable excitement level to a fixed template, substituting only GameEvent fields and matched player data; no generative model shall determine an event, score or player identity.')
fail('AC-AFC-PANEL-01','undefined term; measurability','CHK-RE-25 GLOSSARY_MISMATCH; CHK-RE-47 UNVERIFIABLE','“a labeled default scoring” has no rule table or coefficients in the Glossary, DES-AFC-LINEUP or CONTRACT-AFC-LINEUPSOURCE; a label alone cannot establish correct points.','The lineup panel shall show the selected team’s starters, each player’s fantasy points and game status, and the team total using the league’s Yahoo scoring rules or, for a manual lineup, a default scoring table displayed with the lineup that specifies each counted statistic and its point coefficient; it shall label manual scoring “Default scoring,” mark each value older than stale_after “Stale,” and mark each unavailable value “Unavailable.”')
fail('AC-AFC-PANEL-03','wording','CHK-RE-02 UNOWNED_SUBJECT; CHK-RE-03 WRONG_FORM; CHK-RE-07 OPERATIONS_MIXED','“The customer shall show and hide” obligates the customer rather than the allocated TV component.','The TV app shall let the customer show and hide the lineup panel and select the followed team and league using only the remote’s D-pad, select and back keys, with a visible focus indicator on every focusable element.')
fail('AC-AFC-PANEL-04','wording; measurability','CHK-RE-24 CONTRADICTION; CHK-RE-48 NO_PASS_FAIL','“the panel shall show it within one panel_refresh” applies even when the panel is hidden, although LW-01 stops hidden-panel requests; “panel totals shall agree with the alerts” does not define agreement when alert types, quiet hours or frequency suppress events.','When a starter change or scoring correction reaches the backend, the backend shall include it in subsequent panel responses, and the visible panel shall request those responses every panel_refresh and apply each received response; after being hidden, the panel shall request updated state when shown, and any panel value and released alert referring to the same event shall use the same corrected source facts, irrespective of whether other events produced alerts.')
