fail('AC-AFC-SPIKE-02','allocation; wording','CHK-RE-20 WRONG_LEVEL; CHK-RE-24 CONTRADICTION','“each spike SP-1..SP-6” is allocated wholly to “M2,” which ends 2026-10-15, while SP-6 is explicitly at T_yahoo (2026-10-16) in DES-AFC-SPIKES; the Allocation names lanes only.','The program shall record a verdict file "'`docs/spikes/SP-<n>-<topic>.md` for each spike SP-1..SP-6, containing the route tried, exact steps, evidence paths, verdict and limits, with SP-1..SP-5 complete by M2 exit and SP-6 recorded at T_yahoo.'"', 'Allocation → "'`M2 (SP-1..SP-5), M3 entry at T_yahoo (SP-6); spike verdict records, DeviceAuth/LineupConnector access check`. Keep Source and Verification. This corrects timing; it does not redefine T_yahoo.'"')
fail('AC-AFC-SEC-01','allocation','CHK-RE-20 WRONG_LEVEL; CHK-RE-39 INTERFACE_INCONSISTENT','“keep OAuth tokens only in its DynamoDB table” conflicts with the placement receipt’s LineupConnector constraint “Tokens and client secret are server-side only, in SSM SecureString (TB2).” Neither storage choice is an owner decision.','The APK and every tracked file shall contain no Yahoo client secret, OAuth token, AWS credential or device token; the backend shall read the Yahoo client secret from SSM Parameter Store SecureString and shall keep Yahoo OAuth tokens exclusively in backend storage, without returning them to the TV app.', 'Keep Source, Verification and Allocation. Bind the storage mechanism in the author’s placement/design reconciliation; the requirement fixes the backend-only trust boundary without selecting between the two competing implementation choices. A device bearer token obtained at runtime is not an embedded APK credential.')
fail('AC-AFC-D5-02','wording; traceability','CHK-RE-24 CONTRADICTION; CHK-RE-30 INCORRECT','“no GridMarket identifier (product name …)” also bans the provenance/copyright notice D5-01 and SD-022 require retaining.','The spec-authoring skill’s operational text, templates and tool invocation shall contain no GridMarket product name, document id or "'`--project backend` flag; GridMarket references shall occur only in retained license, attribution and provenance records, and the skill shall contain no absolute local path; building and linting its shipped template in a temporary directory outside any git repository shall exit 0.'"')
