risk_data=[
('01','“Stop device work and return to the owner” is an imperative response, not a bound obligation.','If the stick cannot be located, its API level is below min_sdk, its OS is Fire OS 5 or older, or the provider apps cannot run, then the program shall stop device work and record the condition for the owner without purchasing a device or switching platforms.','SD-001, SD-003, C1, AC-AFC-SPIKE-01','inspection','M2; SP-1 device compatibility verdict and device-work entry control'),
('02','“panel-only presentation remains; owner scope decision” must not silently waive ALERT-04.','If SP-2 cannot demonstrate a heads-up notification over provider playback, then the program shall record the exact device and route limitation, retain panel-only presentation, and record AC-AFC-ALERT-04 as unmet pending an owner scope decision.','#1 Development setup, AC-AFC-ALERT-04','inspection','M2; SP-2 notification verdict and AlertNotifier; M3; integration acceptance record'),
('03','“Ship the best verified outcome (details or app home)” would silently substitute a weaker result for WATCH-02; #1 explicitly says app launch alone does not satisfy specific-game acceptance.','If SP-3 finds no supported content-level link for a specific game, then the program shall record the verified details-page or app-home outcome and its limitation, prepare the missing-interface proposal for the owner, and retain AC-AFC-WATCH-02 as unmet until a specific-game route is demonstrated or the owner changes its acceptance condition.','#1 App launch and game/channel routing research, AC-AFC-WATCH-01, AC-AFC-WATCH-02','inspection','M2; SP-3 provider-route verdict and ProviderResolver registry; M3; WatchLauncher integration acceptance record'),
('04','“Mode A with labeled footage” does not name an obligated subject.','If SP-4 fails to verify Mode B within spike_panel_max, then the system shall use Mode A under AC-AFC-PANEL-05 and the submission materials shall state that the panel is beside the companion’s sample footage rather than provider playback.','SD-006, SD-006a, C5, AC-AFC-PANEL-05','inspection, demonstration','M2; SP-4 verdict; M3; CompanionPlayer/LineupPanel; M5; submission materials'),
('05','“Switch to labeled replay for the demo” has no binding subject or verification field.','If ESPN responses become unavailable or schema-invalid, then the backend shall apply the rejection and stale-data rules of AC-AFC-FEED-01 and AC-AFC-FEED-03 and use labeled replay for the affected demo segments; the submission checklist shall retain the ESPN-terms decision as an owner-only action.','SD-004, C2, C3, AC-AFC-FEED-01, AC-AFC-FEED-03, AC-AFC-SUB-02','test, inspection','M3; FeedIngest/ReplaySource; M5; submission checklist and demo material'),
('06','“Labeled manual lineup” is not a statement of duty.','If Yahoo access is not approved at T_yahoo, then the system shall provide manual lineup entry from ESPN rosters and label every display of that lineup “Manual lineup” under AC-AFC-PROF-04.','SD-007, C6, AC-AFC-PROF-04','test','M3; LineupConnector (ManualSource), ProfileSettings and LineupPanel'),
('07','“Activate the next approved fallback” needs the confirmed-limit condition and the frozen route/capability boundary.','If a selected route reaches a confirmed usage or rate limit, then the Orchestrator shall record the limit evidence and activate only the next approved fallback in the frozen profile with a class B receipt preserving the selected coverage-assist and Reverify settings, or queue the slice when no approved fallback remains; other invocation, configuration, authentication or runtime errors shall not trigger a route switch.','DEC-AFC-PROFILE-001, frozen profile fallback order, owner route-preservation instructions','inspection','M1–M5; frozen lifecycle binding, dispatch packets and route-activation receipts'),
('08','“Hosted runs stop” does not assign the required response.','If private-repository Actions usage exhausts gh_private_minutes, then the program shall stop hosted workflow runs and retain local gate evidence without enabling paid overage unless the owner authorizes it.','SD-017, C11, AC-AFC-CI-02','inspection','M1–M5; GitHub Actions workflow/budget control and repo gate evidence'),
('09','“Stop the scheduler” does not bind the response to the budget condition or identify verification/allocation.','If the AWS Free-plan limits or credits are exhausted or a deployment would introduce a resource outside AC-AFC-SEC-03, then the program shall stop the affected scheduled work or reject that deployment before a change, and shall make no paid-plan change without the owner’s decision.','SD-005, C4, AC-AFC-SEC-03','test, inspection','M2–M5; backend infrastructure deployment guard and EventBridge scheduler control'),
('10','“Manual mapping override …; correction alert” leaves behavior before a verified identity match implicit.','If the Matcher cannot establish a Yahoo-to-ESPN player identity, then the system shall label that player “Unmatched” and withhold player-attributed points and alerts until a verified mapping is available; when a mapping correction changes an already released player attribution, it shall apply the correction to the affected alert and panel state.','#1 item 3 and Right-side fantasy lineup panel; DES-AFC-LINEUP; AC-AFC-ALERT-03','test','M3; Matcher identity map and LineupPanel; M4; AlertPolicy/PanelService corrections'),
('11','“reaches the public repository” followed by “Remove before merge” describes a response that is already too late for the stated condition.','When a secret, personal account detail or absolute local path is detected in material intended for the public repository, the program shall block its merge or publication until sanitized; if exposure has already occurred, it shall record the affected artifact without reproducing the sensitive value and notify the owner for credential rotation or other protected remediation.','Cross-repo rules 2 and 12, SD-010, C7, AC-AFC-SEC-01, AC-AFC-CI-03, AC-AFC-PATH-01','test, inspection','M1–M5; repo hygiene gate, publication checklist and incident record'),
('12','“Record the gap; git hooks still run” is not a bound capability-gap disposition.','If Muse or AGY exposes no supported pre-tool hook, then the D4 installer shall record that harness as a typed gap with exact capability evidence and retain local git hooks invoking the shared gate, without treating those hooks as proof of the missing harness integration.','SD-021, C13, AC-AFC-D4-04','inspection, demonstration','M2; shared harness hook installer, harness configurations and local git hooks'),
('13','“Fail closed on BLOCK or INDETERMINATE” lacks a bound subject and verification/allocation fields.','Before first use of externally acquired software, the program shall obtain a scan-software-supply-chain receipt for that acquisition, refuse use on BLOCK or INDETERMINATE, and verify the pinned distribution checksum for the Gradle wrapper before executing the downloaded distribution.','Cross-repo rule 10; RISK-AFC-13 Control','inspection','M1–M5; software acquisition receipts and TV app build configuration'),
('14','“Fall back to labeled replay for any segment that misses its window” must not silently count replay as the separately required simultaneous-live-games evidence.','If a planned live-game capture or demonstration window is missed, then the program shall use labeled replay for affected demo segments and record any unmet live-integration obligation separately, without presenting replay as the M3 simultaneous-live-games demonstration.','C2, #1 Judging alignment and Development setup, M3 exit criterion','inspection','M2; FeedIngest fixture capture; M3; live integration record; M5; demo clips'),
('15','“Narrow the descriptions …; never merge two skills” is not a binding control and cites an unapproved reciprocal edit as though it were settled.','If matching and non-matching request checks expose a trigger collision between the D5 skill and "'`use-requirements-system`, then the program shall record the failing requests and repair the D5 trigger boundary under AC-AFC-D5-03; any reciprocal edit to `use-requirements-system` shall follow the OD-AFC-07 disposition recorded at integrated review.'"','SD-022, C10, AC-AFC-D5-03, OD-AFC-07 (pending, not confirmed)','inspection','M1; D5 skill description and trigger-check receipts; shared Requirements System skill description only if OD-AFC-07 authorizes its edit'),
('16','“M2 exit records the slip” cannot establish M2 exit while the required D1 rev 0.1 is absent.','If D5 lands later than planned, then the program shall reschedule D1 after that merge, record the schedule impact, and leave the D1 revision 0.1 M2 exit criterion unmet until delivered, without reverting to the superseded project-local GridMarket kit.','SD-022 superseding SD-013, AC-AFC-SPEC-01, M2 exit criterion','inspection','M1; D5 landing receipt; M2; D1 specification and milestone exit record')]
for num,defect,statement,source,verification,allocation in risk_data:
    uid='RISK-AFC-'+num
    fail(uid,'wording; traceability; measurability; allocation','CHK-RE-01 AMBIGUOUS_MODALITY; CHK-RE-17 INCOMPLETE; CHK-RE-20 WRONG_LEVEL; CHK-RE-28 UNTRACEABLE; CHK-RE-47 UNVERIFIABLE',defect+' The actual row schema is Risk / Control / Response, with no Source, Verification or Allocation cells.',statement,f'Source → "'`{source}`. Verification → `{verification}`. Allocation → `{allocation}`. Preserve the original risk description as rationale; promote the proposed control to the Statement field.'"')
notes={
'AC-AFC-PROF-01':'Device-link display/bind flow, device_code_ttl and backend-only Yahoo token boundary are observable; M3 components match placement.',
'AC-AFC-PROF-02':'League/team selection and starter/bench/unknown classification use current-week selected positions; observable backend/TV outputs.',
'AC-AFC-PROF-03':'Package detection, Unknown subscription default and customer overrides have distinct observable states; no entitlement inference.',
'AC-AFC-PROF-04':'T_yahoo condition and Manual lineup label are exact; source and M3 ManualSource/ProfileSettings allocation agree.',
'AC-AFC-MON-01':'Followed-player/game/viewing-period conditions bound eligible fetches; feed_poll_interval is defined; backend request record is observable.',
'AC-AFC-MON-02':'Per-game maximum fetch count over feed_poll_interval is independent of follower count and observable.',
'AC-AFC-MON-03':'Opt-in, unsupported detection message and profile-derived labeling are explicit; SP-2 includes current-playback context.',
'AC-AFC-MON-04':'No alert requests outside enabled viewing periods is observable at AlertService; schedule definition is in Glossary.',
'AC-AFC-FEED-03':'feed_fail_limit, stale state and exact replay label are defined; failure and replay are separately observable conditions.',
'AC-AFC-ALERT-01':'Event relevance and truthful red-zone wording are observable; red_zone_entry/close_game meanings resolve through GameEvent and DES-AFC-FEED.',
'AC-AFC-ALERT-02':'Duplicate, spoiler-delay, quiet-hour and per-game gap rules are observable in release records; zero alert_min_gap means no minimum spacing.',
'AC-AFC-ALERT-03':'A correction references a released alert and changes its panel state; “release” remains subject to ALERT-02 policy, not an unconditional immediate bypass.',
'AC-AFC-WATCH-01':'Launch-target alternatives and unknown-access labeling are explicit; ProviderResolver matches placement.',
'AC-AFC-WATCH-02':'Confirmation and allow-listed intent are observable; GAME_OPENED requires one actual specific-game demonstration. RISK-03 is repaired, not this accepted need.',
'AC-AFC-WATCH-03':'Absent package/failed intent requires an outcome plus reason and forbids success; test can observe both.',
'AC-AFC-CTRL-01':'All listed remote controls and next-decision effect are observable; M4 requires the complete set, with M3 core elaborated by the plan.',
'AC-AFC-CTRL-02':'Restart and reboot persistence has a directly comparable before/after settings state.',
'AC-AFC-CTRL-03':'Conditional visibility requires implemented and device-verified voice; C8 is preserved.',
'AC-AFC-PANEL-02':'Remote device demonstration/inspection can establish simultaneous panel/video, aspect ratio and no crop/overlap; no benchmark required.',
'AC-AFC-PANEL-05':'Bounded Mode B/Mode A verdict, exact footage label, license and README credit are observable; planned fallback matches C5.',
'AC-AFC-SEC-02':'Named public bootstrap routes are exceptions; protected-route missing/invalid token response and absence of mutation are observable. This is not an authorization-design certification.',
'AC-AFC-SEC-03':'Named resource families and refusal before deploy mutation give an observable allow-list check; Free-plan cost is separately controlled by RISK-09.',
'AC-AFC-SEC-04':'Requested Yahoo read scope is inspectable; LineupConnector allocation and read-only source agree.',
'AC-AFC-LW-01':'Thread placement, changed-row rendering and hidden-panel polling cessation are inspectable; publication excludes physical-device performance figures.',
'AC-AFC-D5-01':'Shared skill contents, size bounds, script invocation, environment independence and MIT notice are observable deliverable properties.',
'AC-AFC-D5-03':'Matching/non-matching requests and the non-trigger/checklist-reference text are observable; lint line 37 is inapplicable library-neutrality advice.',
'AC-AFC-D5-04':'Vendor destination, provenance and refusal to overwrite modified files are explicit and observable.',
'AC-AFC-CI-01':'One entrypoint and same area selection across callers, with nonzero failing areas, can be demonstrated by the named test method.',
'AC-AFC-CI-02':'Workflow fields, check names, pins, permissions, fork isolation and runner selection are observable; lint line 46 does not override SD-017/021.',
'AC-AFC-D4-01':'Gate contract/template/installer, common Actions entrypoint, absence of TODO and skill size are observable; lint line 49 does not override SD-017/021.',
'AC-AFC-D4-02':'Guide/checker and size are observable; its budget rule concerns workflow configuration and C11 response, not a claim that a static checker measures account consumption.',
'AC-AFC-D4-03':'Presence/absence of either Vnv root gives run/REFUSED_NO_VNV; GATES rows are lookup data, not repository exclusions (DES-AFC-D4).',
'AC-AFC-D4-04':'C13 ordering, actual hook capability, exact typed-gap evidence and Muse skill exposure are observable; absent capability is never passing evidence.',
'AC-AFC-D4-05':'PR merge form and matching/non-matching skill exercise receipts are inspectable; D4/M1 allocation is a defined component group.',
'AC-AFC-D4-06':'No repository/owner/pilot/exclusion may scope D4 capability; text inspection distinguishes lookup data from scope restrictions.'}
